<BaseLayout title="ECUs & Tuning" description="Holley Terminator X power, Holley dash mounting, and wiring the T56 VSS for speedometer on LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>ECUs &amp; Tuning</h1>
  <p>Holley Terminator X is the most common standalone in the Gen Coupe LS community.</p>
  <nav class="toc">
    <a href="#power">ECU power</a>
    <a href="#dash">Holley dash</a>
    <a href="#speedo">Speedo / VSS</a>
    <a href="#fans">Fan control</a>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="power">12V Power While Cranking</h2>
  <p>
    The Holley needs 12V while cranking: driver's-side fuse box, 2nd row, third down, labeled <em>ECU power</em>.
    Photo and details on the <a href="/guides/wiring#holley-power">Wiring</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="dash">Holley Dash</h2>
  <p>
    I made a simple 90° L bracket to mount the Holley dash. With this setup I can tint the OEM bezels to dim the backlights and still see the fuel level gauge
    without rewiring it into the dash. Pushing the steering wheel up holds the dash in place nicely. Cut a hole in the base panel right behind the dash so you can
    route the harness down behind the dashboard.
  </p>
  <div class="figs">
    <Figure src="holley-dash-cluster.jpg" alt="Holley dash mounted in front of OEM cluster" caption="Dash on the L bracket." />
    <Figure src="holley-dash-interior.jpg" alt="Interior view with Holley dash installed" caption="Interior view." />
    <Figure src="holley-dash-driving.jpg" alt="Driver view of Holley dash while driving" caption="From the driver's seat." />
    <Figure src="holley-dash-fuel-gauge.jpg" alt="OEM fuel gauge still visible behind Holley dash" caption="OEM fuel gauge still visible." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="speedo">Adding Speedo to the Holley Dash (T56)</h2>
  <div class="note">
    <p>This <strong>only</strong> works with the Terminator X Max. <strong>Update:</strong> on the new V3 software you don't need to do this — there's a dropdown setting specifically for the T56 Magnum.</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    To see vehicle speed on the Holley dash or feed it to the ECU, either run the
    <a href="https://www.holley.com/products/fuel_systems/fuel_injection/modules_and_sensors/parts/554-140" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Holley GPS add-on (554-140)</a>
    or wire the trans VSS to the ECU.
  </p>
  <p>
    To wire in the VSS, wire a 2-pin VSS connector to pins <strong>B14 (ground)</strong> and <strong>B18 (signal)</strong> of a J4 connector.
    Then add the Transmission ICF in Holley and set:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Select 4L80 trans</li>
    <li>Enter custom trans gear ratios</li>
    <li>Enter tire size</li>
    <li>Enter <strong>1.17</strong> as the rear end ratio for the T56 Magnum XL</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>VSS Conversion Math</h3>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>4L80 VSS teeth</td><td>40</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tremec Magnum XL VSS teeth</td><td>12</td></tr>
      <tr><td>40 / 12</td><td>3.333</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Diff ratio / 3.333 (e.g. 3.91 / 3.333)</td><td><strong>1.173</strong> — enter as the new diff ratio</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="figs">
    <Figure src="holley-j4-vss-connector.jpg" alt="Holley J4 connector with VSS pigtail" caption="J4 connector with VSS pigtail." />
    <Figure src="holley-transmission-speed-setup.jpg" alt="Holley Terminator X transmission speed calibration screen" caption="Transmission ICF speed setup." />
    <Figure src="holley-vss-forum-note.jpg" alt="Holley forum post about VSS on J4 B18" caption="Holley forum note on VSS input." />
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://a.co/d/gPAob6s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Holley EFI J4 connector kit</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://a.co/d/5YkYHnv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Muzzy's T56 pigtail set (back-up lamp, reverse lockout, VSS)</a></li>
